														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1453499">
									

<p>There are several scientific problems in the article and also poor grammar and use of words.</p>
<p>In the containment procedures it says &quot;one two&quot;</p>
<p>I tihnk personnel is a plural</p>
<p>You don't measure the radioactivity of an object in Sieverts, that's how you measure the absorbed dose of a human (it has a per kilo factor, and also is a weighted dose factoring in the effect of different types of radiation whereas a scientific organisation like this would list the individual energy rates of alpha vs beta vs gamma)</p>
<p>It would probably be pretty difficult to determine the decay chain (possible but you're talking about the sort of equipment at CERN I think, calorimeters), and if it's not emitting gamma, you wouldn't categorise it as a particular chain it must be something else.</p>
<p>xenon should be capitalised</p>
<p>it's should be its</p>
<p>I'm a newb so maybe this is standard but why does the experiment log lead to an incident log and experiment log, also the numbers are weird?</p>
<p>Having to keep things lit or they kill stuff has been done to death imo, worthy of a place on the list of &quot;things wat..&quot;</p>

